WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.220
The Evidence Data Bureau offers aggregated evidence benchmarks for institutional analysis.

2
00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:17.042
Comparable records are grouped by origin, sector, method version and defined boundary to show grade distributions, data completeness and revocation patterns.

3
00:00:17.042 --> 00:00:22.537
Cohort-size rules and anonymisation help prevent a supplier from being re-identified.

4
00:00:22.537 --> 00:00:26.938
Most importantly, the rating entity cannot be the data seller.

5
00:00:26.938 --> 00:00:35.076
Commercial benchmarks operate through a legally separated data business with its own governance, revenue and disclosure.

6
00:00:35.076 --> 00:00:42.094
Fees are fixed subscriptions, never commissions on grade changes, loan approvals or claim denials.

7
00:00:42.094 --> 00:00:49.764
Product availability depends on lawful data use and adequate cohorts; no customer adoption is implied.
